# Campaign specs referenced by docs/guides/QUICKSTART.md. `data/*` above hides
# the directory outright, and git will not descend into an excluded directory,
# so the later `!data/**/*.yml` rule cannot reach these files on its own.
!data/campaigns/
!data/campaigns/**
# 2026-08-27 (Wave J1). THE ADVERTISED SUITE WAS NOT REPRODUCIBLE FROM A CLEAN
# CHECKOUT. `data/*` above excluded three directories that tracked code and tests
# import by absolute path, so the "1245 passed, 0 failed" figure was a property of
# one working tree rather than of the repository.
#
# MEASURED, not estimated (an earlier draft of this comment asserted 13 failures;
# that number was never measured and was wrong). Method: materialise the git INDEX
# with `git checkout-index -a --prefix=<tmp>/` and run
# `python -m pytest tests/unit tests/scientific tests/integration tests/scripts -q`
# in it, so the result reflects what a `git clone` gets and not the working tree.
#   BEFORE this un-ignore: 5 failed, 1238 passed, 4 skipped, 2 xfailed.
# The same 5 are exactly what CI had been reporting all along (run 33037645105,
# job "Unit tests"): 3 in test_authority_benchmark_data.py, 1 in test_data_ingest.py,
# 1 in test_deep_research_tracker.py -- every one a FileNotFoundError or a missing
# fixture, none of them a real defect in the code under test.
#
# Each of these needs the same two-line idiom as
# data/campaigns/ (un-ignore the directory, then its contents) because git does
# not descend into an excluded directory to evaluate a deeper negation.
#   * data/qm/                 -> src/authority_benchmark_data.py,
#                                 tests/benchmarks/_lane_policy.py (40K)
#   * data/ingest_templates/   -> tests/unit/test_data_ingest.py, and the CSV
#                                 templates for the QUICKSTART walkthrough (12K).
#                                 Note these are .csv, which line 30 ignores
#                                 globally; the negation below is what re-includes
#                                 them, and it must therefore stay after it.
#   * data/Gemini_Deep_Research/ -> cited as provenance by src/matrix_correction.py,
#                                 src/barrier_constants.py and the data/lit
#                                 registries (3.1M). Tracked so the citation
#                                 contamination the audit found is REVIEWABLE at
#                                 its source. Read data/Gemini_Deep_Research/README.md
#                                 before trusting a single number in it.
!data/qm/
!data/qm/**
!data/ingest_templates/
!data/ingest_templates/**
!data/Gemini_Deep_Research/
!data/Gemini_Deep_Research/**

